# High-Level Analysis — US-136572
## [CR] [EPQ] MPS Inbound and Outbound — New Fields

**Date:** November 19, 2026
**Story:** US-136572
**Application:** LeretaNetMPSAPI (Manual Procurement Queue API) and the LASTax / LASOutsourcing databases
**Scope:** Exception Processing Queue items sent to MPS — DIR and DMU
**Status:** Analysis only. Nothing has been implemented. The payload format from Common Services is still a draft, so the field names below can change.

---

## 1. Overview

### What the story asks for

Today, when an Exception Processing Queue (EPQ) task is sent to the Manual Procurement service (MPS), four values that processors work with are not part of the message. The story adds them in both directions:

| Field | Sent to MPS (outbound) | Received back from MPS (inbound) |
|---|---|---|
| Bill Number | New | Already works today |
| P&I (penalties and interest) | New | Already works today |
| Payment Status | New | Already works today |
| Follow-up Date | New | New |

### Terms used in this document

- **Outbound** — our API sends a task to MPS.
- **Inbound** — MPS sends the finished task back to our API, and we save the values to the EPQ.
- **Task's own record** — the tax year and installment the task was raised for (the "Details" block on the EPQ screen).
- **Prior installment lines** — the rows in the Delinquency / Prior Information panel on the EPQ screen, one per tax year and installment.

### Expected outcome

- MPS processors see the Bill Number, P&I, Payment Status and Follow-up Date that LERETA already holds for a task.
- When MPS returns a task, the Follow-up Date it sends is saved on the EPQ task, in addition to the three values that are already saved today.
- A task that has none of these values is still sent to MPS as it is today.

### Problem being addressed

MPS processors currently have to work without information LERETA already has, and a follow-up date entered in MPS is lost when the task comes back.

---

## 2. Solution

### 2.1 What will change, in plain words

**Sending to MPS (outbound)**

- Each task sent to MPS will carry the four new values.
- Bill Number, P&I and Payment Status are sent **per installment**: once for the task's own record, and once for every prior installment line. This follows the PO's answer that P&I and Bill Number exist on the prior installments and must be pushed for each of them.
- Follow-up Date is held once per task, so it is sent on the task's own record only.
- When a value does not exist, it is sent as empty (`null`). The task is still sent.

**Receiving from MPS (inbound)**

- Bill Number, P&I and Payment Status coming back from MPS are already saved to the EPQ today. No change is needed; they will be verified by tests.
- Follow-up Date is new. When MPS sends it, we save it on the task.
- The task is still completed, exactly as today. MPS only sends back completed tasks, so a follow-up date does not move the task into Follow-Up status.

### 2.2 Where each value comes from and goes to

| Field | Outbound: task's own record | Outbound: prior installment lines | Inbound: saved to |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bill Number | The task's "Bill No." field (the DIR screen has it; the DMU screen does not, so for DMU it is normally empty) | The Bill No. of that installment line | Already saved today (task record and installment line) |
| P&I | Empty — the task's own record has no P&I. If the panel has a line for the same tax year and installment, that line's P&I is used | The P&I of that installment line | Already saved today (installment line) |
| Payment Status | Paid → `1`, Delinquent → `0`, anything else → empty | The payment code of that installment line (`1` / `0`), empty when blank | Already saved today (task record and installment line) |
| Follow-up Date | The task's follow-up date. If the task has none, the most recent follow-up date from the task's follow-up notes | Not sent (held per task only) | **New:** the task's tracking record, plus a history entry |

### 2.3 Decisions already made

| Topic | Decision | From |
|---|---|---|
| Scope | DIR and DMU only | Developer / story |
| Inbound follow-up date and task status | The task is completed regardless of the follow-up date | PO / Lead |
| Where the inbound follow-up date is saved | On the task's tracking record with a history entry; no follow-up note is created | Developer (to be confirmed by PO / Lead) |
| Outbound follow-up date source | Task's follow-up date first, otherwise the latest follow-up note date | Developer (to be confirmed by PO / Lead) |
| Outbound Payment Status values | `0` / `1` or blank | PO / Lead (MPS accepts these) |
| Outbound P&I | Not on the current record; sent on each prior installment | PO / Lead |
| Outbound Bill Number | Current record's bill number when it has one, and each prior installment's bill number | PO / Lead |

### 2.4 Open points

| # | Open point | Waiting on | What we will do if there is no answer |
