### 2.5 Dependencies and release

- **Depends on US-138600.** The per-installment values travel in the list of installments that US-138600 adds to the payload. The two stories must be built and released together.
- **MPS must be ready.** The payload is a contract with MPS. Our release and theirs have to be coordinated.
- **Order of deployment:** database first, then the API.

### 2.6 What stays the same

- The way tasks are picked up, sent, retried and dead-lettered.
- The inbound handling of Bill Number, P&I and Payment Status.
- The EPQ screens in LERETANet. No screen changes.
- Completion of a task when MPS returns it.

