## 3. Technical Details

### 3.1 Flow reference

- **Outbound:** `DispatcherQuartzJob.Execute` or `GET /api/Dispatcher` → `ProcurementService.GetAllEPQOutboxOrids` → `ProcurementRepository.GetAllEPQOutboxListByIds` (builds the payload) → validation → MPS import endpoint.
- **Inbound:** `POST /api/Receiver` → `InboundAcceptanceService.AcceptAsync` (saves to the inbox) → `InboxProcessor` → `EPQHandler` → `ProcurementService.ExecuteEpqLoanDetailsAsync` → `MapToEpqRequest` → `ProcurementRepository.ExecuteExceptionQueueLoanDetailsUpdAsync` → `usp_ExceptionQueue_Loan_Details_Upd`.

### 3.2 Impacted components

| Component | Item | Change |
|---|---|---|
| MPS contract (outbound) | Installment line of the import payload | Four optional fields: bill number, P&I, payment status, follow-up date. Names per the final Common Services format |
| MPS contract (inbound) | `CsInboundMessage` | New optional `followUpDate` |
| API — DTO | `ManualProcurementQueueAPI.Common/DTOs/MpqOutboundPayload.cs` | Four optional properties on the installment line. No "required" rule, so a missing value never sends the task to dead letter. Bill Number limited to 10 characters |
| API — DTO | `ManualProcurementQueueAPI.Common/DTOs/CsInboundMessage.cs` and the EPQ update request DTO | New follow-up date property |
| API — repository (outbound) | `ProcurementRepository.GetAllEPQOutboxListByIds` | Map Payment Status and Bill Number from the tax-info table (already joined), Follow-up Date from the user-tracking table (already joined) with a fallback to the follow-up notes table, and P&I / Bill Number per installment line from the tax-year-info table |
| API — repository (inbound) | `ProcurementRepository.ExecuteExceptionQueueLoanDetailsUpdAsync` | Pass the new `@FollowUpDate` parameter |
| API — service (inbound) | `ProcurementService.MapToEpqRequest` | Read `followUpDate` from the message using the existing date parser; an invalid date is ignored with a warning and the rest of the message is still saved |
| API — entities | `LasoutsourcingContext` | New entity and `DbSet` for the follow-up notes table (the tax-year-info entity comes with US-138600) |
| API — endpoints, scheduled job, inbox handler | — | No change to routes, schedule or flow |
| API — configuration | `appsettings*.json` | No new keys |
| Database — LASOutsourcing | New synonym for `LASTax.dbo.tbl_ExceptionQueue_FollowUp_Notes` | Lets the API read follow-up notes. (Synonym for `tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_YearInfo` comes with US-138600) |
| Database — LASTax | `usp_ExceptionQueue_Loan_Details_Upd` (router) | New optional last parameter `@FollowUpDate`, passed on to the DIR and DMU procedures |
| Database — LASTax | `usp_ExceptionQueue_DIR_Loan_Details_Upd`, `usp_ExceptionQueue_DMU_Loan_Details_Upd` | New optional `@FollowUpDate`. When supplied, it is saved to `tbl_ExceptionQueue_UserTracking.FollowUpDate` and recorded in `tbl_ExceptionQueue_History`. Completion logic is not changed |
| Database — tables | — | No new tables or columns. All four values already have columns |
| SQL delivery | `SQL\Deployment-Scripts\<MMDDYYYY>\` | One idempotent deployment script; a `*_TEST.sql` validation script under `Documents` |

### 3.3 Other consumers checked

| Consumer | Impact |
|---|---|
| LERETANet EPQ screen (Save / Complete) | Calls the same router procedure with named parameters, so an optional new last parameter does not affect it. Needs a regression test because the DIR and DMU procedures are shared |
| TSP path of the router procedure | Not changed |
| COP flow | No new COP data. COP is affected only by the payload restructure described in US-138600 |
| SSIS / SSRS | No table or column changes, so no impact expected |

### 3.4 Data notes from DEV (read-only checks, November 2026)

- Payment Status on EPQ tasks holds only `P`, `D` or empty.
- No Bill Number is longer than 10 characters.
- Very few open DIR tasks have any of these values yet: of 8,737 DIR tasks staged to MPS, none has a task-level Bill Number or Payment Status and 3 have a follow-up date. Most DIR tasks will therefore go out with these fields empty.
- Of 645 DMU tasks staged to MPS, 626 have a Payment Status, 447 have an installment line for the task's own year and installment, and 93 have a follow-up date in the follow-up notes.

### 3.5 Rules to respect

- No borrower names, addresses, tax IDs or tokens in new log lines.
- No secrets or connection details in code, tests or documents.
- Unit tests (xUnit) for all changed code.

