## 4. Test Scenarios

| Category | Scenario | How to Test | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| Positive | Outbound — DIR task with a Bill No. | Save a Bill No. on an open DIR task staged to MPS, run the dispatcher, read the stored payload in the outbox | Bill Number appears on the task's own record in the payload |
| Positive | Outbound — Payment Status Paid and Delinquent | Dispatch one task with Paid and one with Delinquent | Sent as `1` for Paid and `0` for Delinquent |
| Positive | Outbound — prior installment with P&I and Bill No. | Dispatch a task whose Prior Information panel has a line with P&I and a Bill No. | That line in the payload carries the same P&I and Bill Number |
| Positive | Outbound — follow-up date on the task | Dispatch a task that has a follow-up date on its tracking record | Follow-up Date is sent on the task's own record |
| Positive | Outbound — follow-up date only in follow-up notes | Dispatch a task with no follow-up date on the tracking record but with dated follow-up notes | The most recent note date is sent |
| Positive | Inbound — follow-up date received | Post a completion to `POST /api/Receiver` with a follow-up date | Task is completed; the follow-up date is saved on the tracking record; a history entry exists |
| Positive | Inbound — Bill Number, P&I, Payment Status | Post a completion with these three values | Values are saved on the task and the installment line, as today |
| Negative | Outbound — none of the four values exist | Dispatch a task with no bill number, P&I, payment status or follow-up date | Fields are sent empty; the task is sent and is not dead-lettered |
| Negative | Outbound — Payment Status is neither Paid nor Delinquent | Dispatch a task with an empty Payment Status | Payment Status is sent empty |
| Negative | Inbound — no follow-up date in the message | Post a completion without the field | Processed as today; the stored follow-up date is not changed |
| Negative | Inbound — follow-up date in a wrong format | Post a completion with an invalid date text | The date is ignored and a warning is logged; all other values are saved and the task is completed |
| Edge Case | Bill Number exactly 10 characters | Dispatch a task with a 10-character Bill No. | Sent unchanged |
| Edge Case | Bill Number longer than 10 characters | Dispatch a task with a longer Bill No. | First 10 characters are sent and the event is logged; the task is not dead-lettered (pending open point 4) |
| Edge Case | P&I of 0.00 versus no P&I | Dispatch one line with P&I 0.00 and one with no P&I | `0` is sent for the first and empty for the second |
| Edge Case | Several follow-up notes with different dates | Dispatch a task with more than one dated follow-up note | The most recent date is sent |
| Edge Case | DMU task (no task-level Bill No. on the screen) | Dispatch a DMU task with Bill No. values on its installment lines only | Bill Numbers appear on the installment lines; the task's own record has none |
| Edge Case | Panel has a line for the task's own tax year and installment | Dispatch such a task | One record for that year and installment, carrying the panel line's P&I (pending open point 7) |
| Regression | LERETANet EPQ screen — Save and Complete | Save and complete a DIR and a DMU task from the screen | Works as before; no error from the changed procedures |
| Regression | Inbound message in today's format | Post a completion exactly as MPS sends it today | Processed as before |
| Regression | COP dispatch and receive | Run the dispatcher for COP items and post a COP completion | COP values are unchanged |
| Regression | Retry and dead-letter behaviour | Force an MPS failure during dispatch | Items are retried or dead-lettered as today |
| Regression | TSP tasks through the router procedure | Save a TSP task from the screen | Works as before |
